"1\n00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,229\nThe Learning Brain. Series 3: Generative AI\n\n2\n00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,416\nEpisode 11\n\n3\n00:00:07,496 --> 00:00:09,626\nTrust, but verify\n\n4\n00:00:12,426 --> 00:00:18,924\nResearchers asked two versions of ChatGPT to write eighty four short literature reviews,\n\n5\n00:00:19,288 --> 00:00:24,852\nthen checked all six hundred and thirty six citations against library databases.\n\n6\n00:00:25,022 --> 00:00:26,275\nWith the older model,\n\n7\n00:00:26,356 --> 00:00:29,592\nfifty five percent of the citations did not exist.\n\n8\n00:00:30,004 --> 00:00:32,626\nWith GPT four, eighteen percent.\n\n9\n00:00:33,175 --> 00:00:35,283\nThe fabricated ones looked real,\n\n10\n00:00:35,310 --> 00:00:38,718\nwith plausible titles, often in real journals.\n\n11\n00:00:38,888 --> 00:00:41,041\nEven among real citations,\n\n12\n00:00:41,282 --> 00:00:43,278\nmany had substantive errors,\n\n13\n00:00:43,448 --> 00:00:48,492\nlike wrong volumes or pages: forty three percent for the older model,\n\n14\n00:00:48,686 --> 00:00:51,008\nand twenty four percent for the newer one.\n\n15\n00:00:51,178 --> 00:00:52,806\nNewer models do better,\n\n16\n00:00:52,982 --> 00:00:56,604\nand tools that search before answering reduce fabrication.\n\n17\n00:00:57,017 --> 00:00:58,628\nBut they do not eliminate it.\n\n18\n00:00:58,798 --> 00:01:00,937\nSo verification is a core skill.\n\n19\n00:01:01,421 --> 00:01:03,770\nIn a study of online evaluation,\n\n20\n00:01:03,998 --> 00:01:09,283\nprofessional fact checkers beat both Stanford students and PhD historians.\n\n21\n00:01:09,682 --> 00:01:11,569\nTheir method was lateral reading: leaving the page,\n\n22\n00:01:11,899 --> 00:01:15,384\nto see what other sources say about it.\n\n23\n00:01:15,554 --> 00:01:18,511\nAsked to find the more reliable of two websites,\n\n24\n00:01:18,826 --> 00:01:20,637\nevery fact checker succeeded,\n\n25\n00:01:20,976 --> 00:01:24,328\nagainst half of the historians and a fifth of the students.\n\n26\n00:01:24,498 --> 00:01:25,304\nA caution.\n\n27\n00:01:25,710 --> 00:01:29,234\nThe citation study used models from twenty twenty three,\n\n28\n00:01:29,388 --> 00:01:31,703\nand the lateral reading study was small.\n\n29\n00:01:32,062 --> 00:01:35,995\nBut the principle holds: fluent output is not evidence.\n\n30\n00:01:36,165 --> 00:01:36,948\nFor teaching.\n\n31\n00:01:37,380 --> 00:01:40,536\nRequire students to verify every AI supplied source,\n\n32\n00:01:40,556 --> 00:01:42,293\nand show how they did it.\n\n33\n00:01:42,887 --> 00:01:45,104\nTeach lateral reading explicitly: leave the page,\n\n34\n00:01:45,385 --> 00:01:48,602\nand check who is behind a claim.\n\n35\n00:01:48,988 --> 00:01:53,544\nAnd set an assignment where AI output contains planted errors to find.\n\n36\n00:01:53,714 --> 00:01:55,061\nFluency is free.\n\n37\n00:01:55,250 --> 00:01:57,115\nVerification is the skill.\n\n"
